WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.872 --> 00:00:04.006
Line 3 is running, and nobody may get hurt.

2
00:00:05.107 --> 00:00:07.429
This module is about working safely,

3
00:00:07.603 --> 00:00:11.028
from risk and controls to a safety culture that learns.

4
00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:13.190
You are the engineer.

5
00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:17.338
With the team lead you keep line 3 safe for a whole shift.

6
00:00:18.354 --> 00:00:22.301
First before you start, with risk and controls and with isolation,

7
00:00:22.476 --> 00:00:24.334
electrical work and permits.

8
00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:27.745
Then the machine itself and what you learn,

9
00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:31.332
with machine safety and with incidents and safety culture.

10
00:00:32.654 --> 00:00:35.162
The first topic is Risk and controls.

11
00:00:35.898 --> 00:00:38.081
A hazard is anything that can do harm.

12
00:00:39.085 --> 00:00:43.079
Risk is how likely that harm is, combined with how bad it would be.

13
00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:48.580
You record the risks of line 3 in the R I E, with a plan of action.

14
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:54.138
Just before the start you check with an LMRA what has changed since that plan.

15
00:00:55.412 --> 00:00:59.394
The second topic is Isolation, electrical work and permits.

16
00:01:00.102 --> 00:01:02.308
Stopping is not the same as isolating.

17
00:01:03.338 --> 00:01:08.354
When the unit jams, you isolate the energy at the switch in the grey cabinet.

18
00:01:09.389 --> 00:01:12.338
Only an appointed person does electrical work,

19
00:01:12.477 --> 00:01:15.797
and risky work such as welding gets a permit to work.

20
00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:21.066
You secure that switch with LOTO, with your own lock and a tag with your name.

21
00:01:22.345 --> 00:01:24.423
The third topic is Machine safety.

22
00:01:25.139 --> 00:01:28.436
Most accidents with machines happen in the danger zone.

23
00:01:29.484 --> 00:01:33.628
A guard keeps people out of it, or stops the motion before they get there.

24
00:01:34.636 --> 00:01:38.293
If you must reach in regularly, you use an interlocked guard.

25
00:01:39.659 --> 00:01:42.724
The fourth topic is Incidents and safety culture.

26
00:01:43.463 --> 00:01:45.530
A near miss teaches you something too.

27
00:01:46.553 --> 00:01:50.233
You report it without blame, and then it gives you free lessons.

28
00:01:51.278 --> 00:01:56.119
After an incident you do an incident investigation, which does not look for blame.

29
00:01:57.111 --> 00:02:01.093
That is how you and the team lead keep line 3 safe, all shift.

30
00:02:02.427 --> 00:02:03.216
The whole map.

31
00:02:03.954 --> 00:02:08.064
The fourth station is Safety on the floor, in Keeping the plant running.

32
00:02:09.078 --> 00:02:11.272
Each of the four topics has four levels.

33
00:02:12.316 --> 00:02:16.588
Start at Basics level with hazard, risk and the order of controls.

34
00:02:17.279 --> 00:02:18.881
The rest builds on that.

35
00:02:19.917 --> 00:02:22.494
At Working knowledge level come stopping work,

36
00:02:22.692 --> 00:02:25.920
electrical roles, machine risk and human error.

37
00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:30.703
At Advanced level come the Swiss cheese model, the permit to work,

38
00:02:30.843 --> 00:02:33.455
safety functions and safety indicators.

39
00:02:34.499 --> 00:02:37.018
At Expert level come management of change,

40
00:02:37.146 --> 00:02:40.165
arc flash, old machines and the culture ladder.

41
00:02:41.198 --> 00:02:45.250
Every lesson and every film in this module has a place on this map.
